{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And He said</b> יִשְׁרְצוּ is an intransitive verb, and like it \"and the river shall swarm with frogs\" (Exodus 7:28). The sense of יִשְׁרְצוּ is bringing forth offspring with elevation, and Scripture says that the birds shall fly upon the face of the raqia, as testimony to the meaning of raqia. The Gaon [Saadia] said that עַל פְּנֵי is like עִם פְּנֵי; if so, the faces of the sky are below, and יְעוֹפֵף is like כָּנוּן — \"until He establishes it\" (Isaiah 62:7)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviated epithet פ\"א to פְּנֵי (face of), reading the phrase as 'the face of the sky is below'; alternatively פ\"א may stand for פֵּרֵשׁ אַחֵר (another explained), in which case the clause introduces a different opinion."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:40.496476849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}